			"Message": "feat(Mountain): implement terminal I/O, secret storage, and UI dialogs in CocoonService\n\nReplace unimplemented stubs with working implementations:\n- Terminal I/O: terminal_input sends bytes to PTY stdin via SendTextToTerminal, close_terminal disposes PTY via DisposeTerminal\n- Secret Storage: get_secret/store_secret/delete_secret delegate to OS keychain via SecretProvider (GetSecret, StoreSecret, DeleteSecret)\n- UI Dialogs: show_quick_pick presents selection list via ShowQuickPick, show_input_box presents text entry via ShowInputBox\n- Terminal Resize: emits Tauri event 'sky://terminal/resize' to Sky for xterm.js canvas resizing\n\nAll operations now properly call their corresponding MountainEnvironment providers instead of returning Status::unimplemented, completing the gRPC service contract between Mountain and Cocoon.",
			"SHA": "bd2d00daeba4658e3f694681daf253c64403a113"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-05T13:30:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Implement language provider registration and gRPC service layers\n\nUpdate Grove, Mountain, and Wind submodules with coordinated feature implementations:\n\n**Grove (VS Code API Facade):**\n- Add ProviderStore with atomic handle allocation for tracking active language provider registrations\n- Refactor Disposable to support callback invocation (FnOnce on dispose) for proper lifecycle management\n- Implement all 18 register_*_provider methods with actual registration instead of no-op Disposables\n- Add set_language_configuration registration support\n- Add active_registration_count() for debugging\n\n**Mountain (Rust Backend):**\n- Implement all CocoonService gRPC stubs with working functionality\n- File system operations: read_file, write_file, stat, readdir, delete_file, rename_file, copy_file, create_directory using tokio::fs\n- find_files with glob pattern matching via globset crate\n- git_exec spawning native git process with stdout/stderr capture\n- open_terminal wired to MountainEnvironment TerminalProvider\n- Command registration/unregistration wired to CommandExecutor\n- All 15+ language feature provider registration methods store metadata in ApplicationState\n- Workspace folders initialization from init payload\n- Extension queries via ExtensionManagementService\n\n**Wind (TypeScript Service Layer):**\n- Implement Live service layers for Commands, Editor, Extensions, Files, and Language\n- CommandsService: Local handler registry with IPC delegation to Mountain\n- EditorService: Editor state via Ref subscriptions with Monaco command delegation\n- ExtensionsService: Extension discovery and activation via Mountain IPC\n- FilesService: Full filesystem operations with URI → path normalization\n- LanguageService: In-memory provider registration with local disposal\n- All services use Effect-TS patterns with proper error modeling\n\n**Maintain:** Submodule updates for CI/CD improvements\n\nThis completes the gRPC service contract between Mountain and Cocoon, enabling full language provider support and filesystem operations from the extension host.",
			"SHA": "2d0d95417c08c3a53f30ed7cc029f2723eb7ec17"
		},
